What I changed
- Debug visibility in generated recipes:
  - Embedded a timestamped banner in every recipe including:
    - Latest Spack install log path, selected version, artifact, and dependency summaries.
    - A concise variant_names line to quickly scan extras present.
  - Added a -debug flag and PY_PKG_CREATOR_DEBUG env toggle; when enabled, a session log path is included in the recipe header.
- Correct, Spack-friendly dependency specs:
  - All dependency constraints are normalized to Spack ranges (e.g., >=1.2 => @1.2:).
  - Fixed common version typos from metadata (e.g., 0-24-2 => 0.24.2) before writing.
  - Ensured single-element type tuples include the required trailing comma (e.g., type=("build",)).
  - Always add a python dependency; use precise python@... when Requires-Python is known, otherwise fall back to a default python dep.
- Robust cycle avoidance and recursion:
  - Recursively generate local recipes for missing PyPI deps first, then filter direct two-node cycles by inspecting local recipes.
  - Improved cycle detection to catch versioned depends_on entries, not just plain package names.
- Template accuracy:
  - Normalize pypi path to the Spack “name/name-@<suffix>” format, auto-detecting the suffix from the chosen artifact filename.
  - Keep import_modules to smoke test import after install.
- Tests updated:
  - Assert tuple formatting and pypi path normalization.
  - Added a test ensuring cycle detection recognizes depends_on("py-foo@...") lines.
  - Covered normalization for hyphenated numeric versions.

How to use the new debugging (no need to run now)
- Enable verbose logs via -debug or PY_PKG_CREATOR_DEBUG=1; the generated recipe will include a pointer to the session log in logs/.
- Each recipe now carries a compact, high-signal debug block capturing selection and dependency decisions.

Summary
- Improved recipe correctness and Spack spec normalization.
- Added embedded, always-on debug banner in each generated recipe.
- Hardened direct-cycle filtering and recursion behavior.
- Tests updated to guard the fixes.[?25h[build] compiling py-package-creator...
