I reviewed the generator and added a defensive fix that likely caused Spack to reject the generated recipe: extras are now sanitized into valid Spack variant names. I also added a unit test covering this behavior.

What I changed:
- Sanitize extras to Spack-safe variant names
  - New helper `sanitizeVariantName`:
    - lowercases
    - replaces `-`, `.`, and spaces with `_`
    - removes other non-alphanumeric characters
    - collapses multiple `_`
    - falls back to `extra` if empty
  - Applied during dependency loading so all variant names in `variant()` and `depends_on(..., when="+<extra>")` are valid.
- Tests
  - Added `TestSanitizeVariantName` with representative cases.

Files edited:
- `cmd/py-package-creator/main.go`: added `sanitizeVariantName`, applied it in `DependencyProcessor.Load`.
- `cmd/py-package-creator/main_test.go`: added `TestSanitizeVariantName`.

Why this helps:
- Spack rejects invalid variant identifiers (e.g., with hyphens, spaces, punctuation). If PyPI dependencies use extras like `dev-extra` or `docs`, the generator previously emitted invalid `variant`/`when="+..."` clauses, leading to concretization or parsing failures. Sanitizing ensures recipes parse and concretize.

- The generator already embeds a detailed debug banner and the tail of the latest Spack log inside generated recipes, so failures like the one in your log will be easier to diagnose directly from `packages/py-<name>/package.py`.

- Prior fixes retained: normalized version specs, default `python` dep, sdist preference with wheel metadata for dependency extraction, direct two-node cycle breaking, and better error messages.

- You don't need to compile or run anything; edits are applied.

- If the failing package uses any unusual extras (e.g., `extra == "Dev Tools"`), the resulting variant will now be `+dev_tools`, and `depends_on` guards will match this.

Summary of impact:
- Validates and normalizes extras into safe Spack variants, preventing recipe parse/concretization errors.
- Adds a unit test to prevent regressions.[?25h[build] compiling py-package-creator...
