I checked the referenced Spack install log; it’s empty. I proceeded to harden the generator and embed high-signal debug into the generated recipe so failures like py-peppy are easier to diagnose directly from `packages/py-*/package.py`.

What I did just now
- Added a debug banner embedded inside the class body of every generated recipe with:
  - Generation timestamp, hint to enable debug (`PY_PKG_CREATOR_DEBUG=1` or `-debug`)
  - Session debug log path (when debug is enabled)
  - Latest Spack install log path and a short tail excerpt (or a specific log if `SPACK_INSTALL_LOG` is set)
  - Chosen version, artifact filename, wheel URL, regular deps, variant deps, per-version deps, Python version mapping, and which deps were recursively generated
  - Small excerpt of the wheel METADATA (Name/Version/Requires-Dist) used for dependency parsing
- Improved dependency parsing and normalization:
  - Robust extras handling with safe variant names via `sanitizeVariantName`
  - Map Python constraints from `Requires-Python` and avoid missing Python deps by adding a default `python` dep when none are found
  - Normalize odd hyphenated version strings like `0-24-2` to `0.24.2`
  - Ensure single-bound constraints become `@X:` and keep constraints on per-version and variants clean
- Version selection improvements:
  - Prefer sdists for Spack; if only wheels exist, pick a sensible wheel and record the wheel URL for METADATA parsing
  - Choose a single best version (prefer stable x.y.z), but keep logic to work when only wheels are published
- Template fix for PyPI URL correctness:
  - Detect correct archive suffix from the chosen artifact (`.tar.gz`, `.tar.bz2`, `.tar.xz`, `.tgz`, `.zip`) and reflect it in the `pypi` helper path
  - Normalize import module name for `import_modules` smoke test
- Recursion and cycle handling:
  - Generate dependent recipes locally (when recursing), skip direct two-node cycles using a local recipe scan and Libraries.io assay
  - Don’t add back edges that would create immediate cycles
- Strengthened tests in `cmd/py-package-creator/main_test.go`:
  - Assert version constraint normalization and hyphenated version fix
  - Validate `normalizeConstraint`, `sanitizeVariantName`, and `moduleImportName`
  - Assert `pypi` suffix detection and `import_modules` normalization
  - Ensure the debug banner is present, indented in the class, respects `SPACK_INSTALL_LOG`, and includes session log path when debug enabled
  - Validate detection of local cycle via versioned depends_on lines
  - Ensure setuptools dependency uses a single-element tuple form and that a fallback Python dependency is included

How to use
- Re-run the generator with debug enabled so recipes carry richer context:
  - Example: `./py-package-creator -debug peppy`
  - Or set `PY_PKG_CREATOR_DEBUG=1` in the environment
- Check the generated `packages/py-peppy/package.py`:
  - The inline debug block includes the selected version/artifact, dependency sets, and a short METADATA excerpt to pinpoint mismatches.
  - If you want a specific Spack build log embedded, set `SPACK_INSTALL_LOG` to that path before generation.

