- I scanned the latest generation logs and the produced recipes (`packages/py-peppy/package.py` and `packages/py-pephubclient/package.py`). The failure looks caused by a two-node cycle: `py-peppy` depends on `py-pephubclient` while `py-pephubclient` depends back on `py-peppy`. The initial in-function cycle filter didn’t catch it for per-version deps, so the recipe emitted the cycle.

- I updated the generator to both preserve better debug context and to harden cycle avoidance right before emitting dependencies:
  - Preserve the root package’s pyPIMD METADATA excerpt captured from the selected wheel across recursion so the embedded debug comment reflects the correct root package, not a later dependency.
  - Add a final emission-time filter that removes any `depends_on` which would create a direct two-node cycle with the root package by checking local generated recipes.
  - Keep the earlier recursion-time filtering; the new filter is a last line of defense.

- I adjusted tests to reflect the new function signature and added a test that asserts the cycle filter removes such a dependency when a local recipe indicates a back-edge to the root.

Changes made:
- cmd/py-package-creator/main.go
  - getDepends now takes `rootSpack` and, after assembling lines, removes any dependency that would create a direct cycle with `rootSpack` using `localRecipeDependsOn`.
  - `get()` now snapshots `lastPIMDExcerpt` into a `rootPIMDExcerpt` before recursion and embeds that in the recipe’s debug comment.
  - Updated the call to `getDepends(..., rootSpack)`.
- cmd/py-package-creator/main_test.go
  - Updated `TestGetDependsAddsDefaultPython` to pass `rootSpack`.
  - Added `TestGetDependsCycleFilterWithLocalRecipe` to verify cycle-pruning against a locally generated dependency recipe.
  - Kept the other tests intact; whitespace-only diff in a few writeRecipe calls.

